      "4 days ago",
      "Chip stocks extend pullback, but pare some losses after jobs data",
      "The chip sector was extending its pullback in early trading, but pared some losses in the wake of much stronger than expected jobs data. The VanEck Semiconductor ETF was falling 2.7% in premarket trading, but was down 2.9% just before the data was released.",
      "Still, all 25 of the chip ETF's equity components were trading lower, with Nvidia shares shedding 1.7%, Broadcom's stock dropping 1.8% and Micron's stock down 4.2%. The ETF had fallen 1.6% on Thursday, to pullback from Wednesday's record close, after a strong, but not strong enough, earnings report from Broadcom."
